          "explain": "Down syndrome gathers a flat face, a small head, a small mouth with a protruding tongue, upward slanting eyes, rounded cheeks, and weak floppy muscles, called hypotonia. A long, round, or narrow face is not the face finding. A large, long, or pointed head is not the head finding. A small, absent, or short tongue is not the tongue finding. Downward, lateral, or absent slant is not the eye finding. Sunken, hollow, or pale cheeks are not the cheek finding. Rigid muscles, spasm, and tremor are not the muscle finding."
