          "explain": "Cost/o means rib, as in intercostal. Lumb/o means the loin or lower back, as in lumbar and thoracolumbar. Oste/o means bone, as in osteoarthrotomy. Pelv/i and Pelv/o are the two spellings for the hip bone or pelvic cavity, as in pelvimetry and pelvofemoral. Radi/o and Uln/o name the two forearm bones, the radius and the ulna, jointly seen in radioulnar. Stern/o means the sternum or breastbone, as in sternocostal. The paired forms on the left are synonym spellings or a natural anatomical pair, so each left entry maps to a single right entry."
