          "explain": "The long-bone group is the bones of the arms and legs, and the metacarpals are labeled in that group. Metacarpals are bones of the palm, in the upper limb, so they are appendicular. They are long bones, not short, flat, or irregular. Metacarpels, Metacarples, and Metacarpalls are misspellings. They are not axial. The wrist bones are the carpals, the ankle bones are the tarsals, and the sole bones are the metatarsals.",
