          "explain": "The long-bone group is the bones of the arms and legs, and the metatarsals are labeled in that group. Metatarsals are bones of the sole, in the lower limb, so they are appendicular. They are long bones, not short, flat, or irregular. Metatarsels, Metatarsles, and Metatarsalls are misspellings. They are not axial. The palm bones are the metacarpals, the ankle bones are the tarsals, and the shin is the tibia.",
