          "explain": "This term is hemochromatosis. Hemochromotosis, Hemachromatosis, and Hemochromatasis miss the spelling. Iron overload deposits produce bronze skin pigmentation and can cirrhose the liver. Vein redness and clot after catheter injury fits thrombophlebitis, enlargement of the spleen after congestion is splenomegaly, and absence of the thymus from early life is athymism. The elements are hem/o, chrom, and a condition ending. An inflammation ending would make it an inflammation, hemat/o is not the blood form used in this term, and a tumor ending would name a growth."
