          "explain": "The scalp covers the skull, and the skin covers the sternum. The spinal cord runs inside the vertebral canal, and the marrow fills the inside of a bone under its compact outer layer. The kidneys lie inside the abdomen, under the muscles of the back, while the thigh muscles wrap around the femur. Proximal and distal are about distance along a limb from the trunk, which none of these pairs describes."
